# Line endings are load-bearing for this project.
#
# The device downloads these files STRAIGHT FROM THE GITHUB ARCHIVE and runs them
# with /bin/sh. If a shell script arrives with CRLF endings the kernel looks for
# an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and every script fails with a
# confusing "not found" -- while looking perfectly fine in an editor. So pin LF
# for the repo AND on checkout, whatever core.autocrlf happens to be set to
# locally. (This bit us once already; verify.ps1 now checks for CR as well.)
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
.gitignore        text eol=lf
.gitattributes    text eol=lf

# Images are binary; never touch them.
*.png   binary
